========================================================================
         THE CHRONOLOGICAL GIT OPERATIONS GUIDE FOR DEVOPS
========================================================================

------------------------------------------------------------------------
🌅 ACT 1: THE MORNING SYNC (ARRIVING AT WORK)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git clone <GITHUB_REPO_URL>
-> [LOCAL & REMOTE] Downloads the entire company cloud project from 
   GitHub to your laptop for the very first time.

git checkout main
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Steps your workspace onto your laptop's master timeline.

git pull origin main
-> [LOCAL & REMOTE] Synchronizes your laptop. Sucks down all updates 
   your teammates pushed to GitHub while you were sleeping.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
🌿 ACT 2: SAFE ISOLATION (STARTING YOUR ASSIGNMENT)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git checkout -b <branch-name>
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Splits the timeline! Creates a parallel playground branch 
   and steps inside it so you don't break the working master code.

.gitignore (A hidden text file named exactly this in your main folder)
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Your invisible shield. Write names of secret files 
   inside it (like passwords and API keys). Git promises to ignore them.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
🟡 ACT 3: THE BUILD LOOP (WRITING & SAVING WORK LOCALLY)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git status
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Your dashboard. Shows what changed (Red = unsaved, 
   Green = staged and ready to lock in).

git add .
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Stages your changes. Loads all loose files onto your 
   local launchpad and turns them green.

git commit -m "your description"
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Clicks the camera shutter! Takes a permanent snapshot 
   and logs it into your laptop's history book.

git log --oneline
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Opens your history book to see a clean list of all 
   your successful snapshots.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
🚨 ACT 4: THE MID-DAY CRISIS (THE EMERGENCY SHIFT)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git stash
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Shoves your messy, unfinished branch edits into a secret 
   drawer so your screen is instantly clean to fix an urgent bug.

git stash pop
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Opens the drawer and pulls your messy edits back onto 
   your screen so you can resume your morning work exactly where you left off.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
☁️ ACT 5: THE CLOUD LAUNCH (PUSHING & DEPLOYING)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git push origin <branch-name>
-> [LOCAL & REMOTE] Fires your playground branch timeline up into the 
   GitHub cloud vault.

Open Pull Request (PR) (Done on GitHub.com)
-> [REMOTE ONLY] Asks your team leads to review your playground files 
   before they hit production.

Merge Pull Request (Done on GitHub.com)
-> [REMOTE ONLY] Fuses your feature code into the remote main branch. 
   This triggers your automated scripts to build real servers.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
🌆 ACT 6: END-OF-DAY CLEANUP (LOGGING OFF)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git branch -d <branch-name>
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Demolishes your local playground branch from your 
   hard drive to keep your laptop clean since it is safely backed up in the cloud.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
🛡️ EMERGENCY BUTTONS (IF ANYTHING WENT WRONG)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
git restore --staged <filename>
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Un-stages a file. Takes a green file off the launchpad 
   back to red status.

git reset --soft HEAD~1
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Erases your last local commit snapshot, but leaves your 
   code open and green on your screen so you can quickly edit it.

git reset --hard HEAD
-> [LOCAL ONLY] Total wipeout switch. Destroys all uncommitted edits 
   and warps your folder back to your last clean save.

git revert HEAD
-> [LOCAL & REMOTE] Follow this with a "git push". Creates an opposite 
   commit to cancel out a mistake already live on GitHub without breaking 
   your team's history.

git reflog
-> [LOCAL ONLY] The master black-box log. Used to find and rescue 
   accidentally deleted commits or bad resets.
